================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE — PLEASE READ
================================================================================

This MIT licence covers the ORIGINAL SOURCE CODE of this project only: the
contents of src/, api/, scripts/, tests/, notebooks/, dashboard/ (excluding
third-party packages restored by npm) and the project's own documentation.

It does NOT cover the datasets, the pre-trained pose model, or any third-party
dependency. Those carry their own separate terms, set out below. Do not assume
the code licence extends to the data.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Multimodal Sports Injury Dataset  —  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
File:      data/raw/multimodal_sports_injury_dataset.csv
Source:    https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anjalibhegam/multimodal-sports-injury-dataset
Owner:     anjalibhegam (Kaggle)
Accessed:  6 August 2026
Licence:   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

This licence is NOT compatible with the MIT terms above and is more
restrictive. It imposes three conditions on this dataset and on anything
derived from it:

  BY (Attribution)   — credit the original Kaggle dataset owner.
  NC (NonCommercial) — no commercial use of the dataset or its derivatives.
  SA (ShareAlike)    — adapted versions of the dataset must be redistributed
                       under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, not MIT.

Practical consequences for anyone reusing this repository:

  - The derived files under outputs/injury/ (cleaned, split and engineered
    versions of this dataset) are adaptations and remain CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
  - The trained injury model bundles in models/ and models/baseline/ are derived
    from this data. Treat them as non-commercial-use artefacts.
  - The BWF stream is unaffected by these terms.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. BWF match records  —  researcher-collected, no redistribution licence granted
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
File:            data/raw/bwf_matches_2021_2025.csv
Collection code: https://github.com/ShermaineYap/BWFWebScrap
Source:          publicly accessible BWF web endpoints
                 (https://extranet-lv.bwfbadminton.com/api)
Coverage:        2021-2025 (26,341 raw match records)

These records were collected by the author from publicly accessible BWF pages
for academic research. The underlying facts originate with the Badminton World
Federation, which has not granted any redistribution licence to this project.
The author claims no ownership of the underlying match facts and grants no
licence over them. The COLLECTION CODE is separately licensed at the repository
above; this file records only the provenance of the data.

The BWF tournament calendar (artifacts/bwf_tournament_calendar.json) and the
run-time draw cache come from the same source under the same terms. Neither is
used for training, evaluation or any reported result.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
